# Lane Changing Management with HMM
This repository contains the complete implementation of a Hidden Markov Model (HMM) for risk assessment during lane changing maneuvers on highways. The project includes data preprocessing, feature extraction, model training, and evaluation pipelines using the highD drone dataset.

# Repository Structure
hmm_model.py - HMM implementation with 4 hidden states for risk classification

safety_models.py - Additional models (FSM, RSS, Reg157, CC_human_driver)

data_processor.py - HighD dataset loading, filtering, and synchronization

feature_engineering.py - TTC, DHW, lateral motion intensity calculation

evaluation.py - Metrics, confusion matrices, and visualization

config.py - Hyperparameters and model configuration

# Quick Start
Simply run the main simulation script:

bash
python safety_check_runner.py
This will execute the complete pipeline: load preprocessed data, run the HMM model, perform risk assessment, and display evaluation metrics including accuracy, precision, recall, and F1-score.

